<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's packaging firm profits rise.</title>
<headline>Morocco's packaging firm profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moroccan packaging firm Carnaud Maroc said on Wednesday its profits rose to 31.2 million dirhams in 1996 from 29.7 million dirhams in 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover for 1996 was 570.3 million dirhams from 541.6 million dirhams in 1995.</p>
<p>Casablanca-based Upline Securities said in a recent report that Carnaud was Morocco's leading canning company, handling mainly fish and vegetable exports.</p>
<p>Its shares were last traded in March at 587 dirhams.</p>
<p>($ = 9.2 dirhams)</p>
</text>
